k Progression (conditionality and careers) </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Devolution (Local) </p>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <p>Disability Employment</p>\n  </li>\n</ul>\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":100,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2025-11-18T10:12:45Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Minister of State (Minister for Employment)","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/minister-of-state--203","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-education","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-education","base_path":"/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-education","content_id":"845e63b4-c0f1-11e4-8223-005056011aef","details":{"body":"<p>The Secretary of State is responsible for the work of the Department for Education, including:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>early years and childcare</li>\n  <li>children’s social care</li>\n  <li>teacher quality, recruitment and retention</li>\n  <li>the school curriculum</li>\n  <li>school improvement</li>\n  <li>academies and free schools</li>\n  <li>further education</li>\n  <li>apprenticeships and skills</li>\n  <li>higher education</li>\n</ul>\n\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":16,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2022-11-08T09:31:05Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Secretary of State for Education","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-education","withdrawn":false}],"taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/childcare-parenting/child-poverty","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/childcare-parenting/child-poverty","base_path":"/childcare-parenting/child-poverty","content_id":"eb6c325f-09b7-4873-86f0-6b2eacc4d27f","description":"Information on child poverty, including the work of the Child Poverty Taskforce.","details":{"internal_name":"Child poverty","notes_for_editors":"","url_override":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"parent_taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/childcare-parenting/childrens-health-and-welfare","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/childcare-parenting/childrens-health-and-welfare","base_path":"/childcare-parenting/childrens-health-and-welfare","content_id":"2389dfd4-a0c4-4bd2-b7e6-06f465463d22","description":"Children's rights, child poverty, mental health, young carers, special educational needs and disabilities (SEND).","details":{"internal_name":"Children's health and welfare","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"parent_taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/childcare-parenting","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/childcare-parenting","base_path":"/childcare-parenting","content_id":"206b7f3a-49b5-476f-af0f-fd27e2a68473","description":"Financial support, finding and providing childcare, pregnancy and birth, adoption and fostering, looked-after children, safeguarding.","details":{"internal_name":"Parenting, childcare and childrens services","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":true},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"root_taxon":[{"api_path":"/api/content/","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/","base_path":"/","content_id":"f3bbdec2-0e62-4520-a7fd-6ffd5d36e03a","document_type":"homepage","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-02-18T13:00:23Z","schema_name":"homepage","title":"GOV.UK homepage","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2017-07-27T13:29:23Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Parenting, childcare and children's services ","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/childcare-parenting","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2017-07-27T13:33:54Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Children's health and welfare","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/childcare-parenting/childrens-health-and-welfare","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2025-01-15T15:00:36Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Child poverty","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/childcare-parenting/child-poverty","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2026-03-13T00:01:00+00:00","publishing_app":"whitehall","publishing_request_id":"21-1774858597.814-10.13.20.149-2992","publishing_scheduled_at":"2026-03-13T00:01:00+00:00","rendering_app":"frontend","scheduled_publishing_delay_seconds":7,"schema_name":"news_article","title":"New tool for families and schools to cut stigma of child poverty","updated_at":"2026-08-14T18:27:21+01:00","withdrawn_notice":{}}